OFFLINE_LIBRARY.push(...[{"id":"igopx-writing-9231","type":"writing","title":"Task1 欧洲出生死亡人数","book":"邪21","part":1,"description":"Task 1 · 至少 150 词","minWords":150,"prompt":"The graph below shows the total births and the deaths in a European country from 1950 to 2050.\nSummarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.\nWrite at least 150 words.","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">The graph below shows the total births and the deaths in a European country from 1950 to 2050.<br>Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.<br>Write at least 150 words.<br></div><p><img src=\"./assets/87de5d440e5cc966c4f5fca00b321ec12ccb1e68b399a518104dde97d1bea7f5.png\" title=\"欧洲出生死亡.png\" alt=\"欧洲出生死亡.png\"/></p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website_with_ai_corrections","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"The line graph illustrates changes in the total number of births and deaths in a particular European country between 1950 and 2050.\nOverall, it is evident that the number of deaths remained relatively stable throughout the entire period, while the number of births experienced considerable fluctuations.\nIn 1950, the total number of births stood at just under 800,000. Over the following two decades, this figure rose sharply, reaching a peak of around one million in 1970. However, the trend then declined dramatically to approximately 600,000 in 1990, marking the lowest point over the whole period. According to the projections, the number of births is expected to recover slightly and stabilise at around 700,000 by 2050.\nTurning to the number of deaths, it began at roughly 700,000 in 1950 and remained largely unchanged until 2010. After that, it is predicted that the number of deaths will increase gradually, reaching about 800,000 by the end of the period, at which point it will exceed the number of births.","word_count":171,"revision_notes":["the birth rate is expected → the number of births is expected","the death rate will increase → the number of deaths will increase","it will exceed the birth rate → it will exceed the number of births"]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["概述出生人数先升后降再趋稳，死亡人数长期平稳后上升，末期死亡数超过出生数。","细节一按时间写出生人数的峰值、低点和预测；细节二写死亡人数并比较两条线。","人数用 number of births/deaths；rate 通常指比率。1950至2050含预测，区分过去时与 is projected to。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"rise steadily","meaning_zh":"稳步上升","usage":"rose steadily from A to B"},{"expression":"reach a peak","meaning_zh":"达到峰值","usage":"reached a peak of X"},{"expression":"remain stable","meaning_zh":"保持稳定","usage":"remained stable at X"},{"expression":"fluctuate","meaning_zh":"波动","usage":"fluctuated between A and B"},{"expression":"be projected to","meaning_zh":"预计会","usage":"is projected to rise"},{"expression":"by contrast","meaning_zh":"相比之下","usage":"By contrast, the figure for ..."}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9231&scene=%E5%8A%A8%E6%80%81%E5%9B%BE&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9233","type":"writing","title":"Task1 医疗满意度","book":"邪21","part":1,"description":"Task 1 · 至少 150 词","minWords":150,"prompt":"The graph below shows people's level of satisfaction with the health care system in 4 countries between 1991 and 2007.\nSummarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.\nWrite at least 150 words.","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">The graph below shows people's level of satisfaction with the health care system in 4 countries between 1991 and 2007.<br>Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.<br>Write at least 150 words.<br></div><p><img src=\"./assets/63e9f92b7ad2d2c9e03758c1f68f6a6bfa40641ac5948a654728c35912a78e68.png\"/></p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website_with_ai_corrections","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"The line graph illustrates the level of satisfaction with healthcare systems in four different countries from 1991 to 2007.\nOverall, for most of the timeframe, the Netherlands recorded the highest level of satisfaction, whereas the USA consistently remained at the lowest level.\nFocusing on the two countries with the highest satisfaction levels, Canada ranked first in 1991, with 56% of respondents expressing satisfaction, compared with just under 50% in the Netherlands. The Dutch figure stayed relatively stable at around 50% until 1998, before declining slightly by the end of the period. In contrast, Canada saw a sharp drop to 20% in 1998. However, this was followed by a recovery, with satisfaction levels rising to 30% by 2007.\nBy comparison, satisfaction with the healthcare system in the USA was much lower. In 1991, only 10% of people reported being satisfied, and although this figure increased gradually, it reached only around 16% in 2007. Similarly, the satisfaction rate in the UK began at approximately 27% and showed very little variation throughout the period.","word_count":171,"revision_notes":["around 17% in 2007 → around 16% in 2007"]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["概述荷兰在后两个年份领先、美国一直最低；加拿大变化最剧烈。","将荷兰与加拿大放在一段，英国与美国放在另一段；比较起终值和1998年的转折。","表达调查满意者占比，不解释医疗政策原因。百分比差异写 percentage points。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"rise steadily","meaning_zh":"稳步上升","usage":"rose steadily from A to B"},{"expression":"reach a peak","meaning_zh":"达到峰值","usage":"reached a peak of X"},{"expression":"remain stable","meaning_zh":"保持稳定","usage":"remained stable at X"},{"expression":"fluctuate","meaning_zh":"波动","usage":"fluctuated between A and B"},{"expression":"recover","meaning_zh":"回升","usage":"recovered to X"},{"expression":"by contrast","meaning_zh":"相比之下","usage":"By contrast, the figure for ..."}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9233&scene=%E5%8A%A8%E6%80%81%E5%9B%BE&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9235","type":"writing","title":"Task1 两国男女工作比例","book":"邪21","part":1,"description":"Task 1 · 至少 150 词","minWords":150,"prompt":"The charts show the percentage of male and female workers in country A and country B.\nSummarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.\nWrite at least 150 words.","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">The charts show the percentage of male and female workers in country A and country B.<br>Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.<br>Write at least 150 words.<br></div><p><img src=\"./assets/660d67458b889fcd326dbfeec3d9ae390f39202297f243c0e1a8ad34897ceaf6.png\"/></p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website_with_ai_corrections","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"The pie charts compare the distribution of male and female workers across agriculture, industry and services in Countries A and B.\n\nOverall, services accounted for the largest proportion of workers of each gender in both countries. Agriculture was much more prominent in Country A, whereas Country B had particularly high shares of employment in services, especially among women.\n\nIn Country A, 56% of male workers were employed in services, compared with 49% of female workers. Agriculture represented the second-largest sector for both groups, accounting for 29% of men and 43% of women. Industry had the smallest shares, at 15% for males and 8% for females.\n\nIn Country B, services employed 65% of male workers and an even larger proportion of female workers, at 88%. The figures for industry were 32% and 11% respectively. By contrast, agriculture employed very few workers of either gender: just 3% of men and 1% of women. Compared with Country A, therefore, Country B had a much smaller agricultural share and a greater concentration of female employment in services.","word_count":173,"revision_notes":["AI依据原图重写，纠正男女农业占比与统计分母，移除图中未提供的年份。"]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["概述两国男女均以服务业为最大部门，B国农业占比明显更小。","按国家分段，分别比较男性与女性的行业分布；突出A国女性农业占43%和B国女性服务业占88%。","各饼图的分母是该国该性别工人总数，不能据此推断男女绝对人数。图中未标年份，不添加年份。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"account for","meaning_zh":"占比例","usage":"accounted for X% of ..."},{"expression":"the corresponding figure","meaning_zh":"对应数值","usage":"the corresponding figure for ..."},{"expression":"percentage points","meaning_zh":"百分点","usage":"a gap of X percentage points"},{"expression":"respectively","meaning_zh":"分别","usage":"A and B were X and Y respectively"},{"expression":"the largest proportion","meaning_zh":"最大占比","usage":"recorded the largest proportion"},{"expression":"in comparison with","meaning_zh":"与之比较","usage":"in comparison with ..."}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9235&scene=%E9%9D%99%E6%80%81%E5%9B%BE&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9237","type":"writing","title":"Task1 制作奶酪流程","book":"邪21","part":1,"description":"Task 1 · 至少 150 词","minWords":150,"prompt":"The diagram below shows how soft cheese is made.\nSummarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.\nWrite at least 150 words.","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">The diagram below shows how soft cheese is made.<br>Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.<br>Write at least 150 words.<br></div><p><br/></p><p><img src=\"./assets/58bca18e84c029f320ad4ebf0711c8d692cca3913e6a65e4b3ee727ed6d607f9.png\" title=\"image.png\" alt=\"image.png\"/></p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website_with_ai_corrections","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"The diagram illustrates the production of soft cheese from milk and water.\n\nOverall, the process consists of five main stages, beginning with mixing the ingredients and ending with cooling the cheese. During production, the mixture is cooled, fermented and heated to remove moisture, while filters separate the product from waste water.\n\nFirst, milk and water are poured into a mixing chamber and blended together. The resulting liquid then passes into a cooling chamber, where it is kept at 5 degrees Celsius for two hours. Salt is added before the mixture enters the fermentation stage. Here, it is heated to 37 degrees Celsius and held at this temperature for six hours, becoming thicker as the process continues.\n\nNext, the mixture is transferred to an evaporation chamber. The temperature is raised to 100 degrees Celsius for eight hours, and steam escapes through an outlet. Finally, the product passes through a filter into the last cooling chamber, where it is maintained at 5 degrees Celsius for another eight hours. A further outlet allows waste water to be removed, leaving the finished soft cheese.","word_count":180,"revision_notes":["AI依据原图重写，补足总体段、过滤及废水步骤，纠正流程图名称。"]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["概述五个主要阶段：混合、冷却、发酵、蒸发、最终冷却；原料是牛奶和水。","按箭头顺序说明加盐、温度与持续时间，并说明过滤及废水排出。","用一般现在时与被动语态；首次冷却仅2小时，不重复添加时间；不要将流程图称为table。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"be mixed with","meaning_zh":"与之混合","usage":"milk is mixed with water"},{"expression":"undergo fermentation","meaning_zh":"经历发酵","usage":"the mixture undergoes fermentation"},{"expression":"evaporation","meaning_zh":"蒸发","usage":"the evaporation stage"},{"expression":"be heated to","meaning_zh":"被加热到","usage":"is heated to X degrees Celsius"},{"expression":"be filtered","meaning_zh":"被过滤","usage":"the product is filtered"},{"expression":"subsequently","meaning_zh":"随后","usage":"Subsequently, the mixture ..."}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9237&scene=%E9%9D%99%E6%80%81%E5%9B%BE&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9866","type":"writing","title":"三国用水量","book":"密题范文-小作文","part":1,"description":"Task 1 · 至少 150 词","minWords":150,"prompt":"The charts below show the distribution of the world's water and the use of water in three countries.\nSummarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.\nWrite at least 150 words.","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">The charts below show the distribution of the world's water and the use of water in three countries.<br>Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.<br>Write at least 150 words.<br></div><p><img src=\"./assets/7525588809797ec4a60d8fed203595d0cb6f7b7d285993020503946a00474358.jpg\"/></p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"The charts illustrate how global water is distributed and compare the proportions of water used for three different purposes in Egypt, Saudi Arabia, and Canada.\nOverall, it is clear that the vast majority of the world’s water is salty, while ice and glaciers make up the largest share of freshwater. Additionally, water consumption patterns vary significantly among the countries; Egypt and Saudi Arabia heavily rely on water for agricultural purposes, whereas industrial use dominates in Canada.\nRegarding global water distribution, salt water accounts for 97% of total water, leaving a mere 3% as freshwater. Within this small portion of freshwater, nearly four-fifths (79%) is bound in ice and glaciers, followed by groundwater at 20%. In contrast, surface water constitutes a tiny fraction, representing only 1%.\nIn terms of water consumption, Egypt and Saudi Arabia exhibit strikingly similar trends. Agriculture is by far the largest consumer of water in both nations, accounting for roughly 79% in Egypt and 78% in Saudi Arabia. Domestic use forms the second largest sector at around 14% for both countries, while industry consumes the smallest proportion, at under 10%. Conversely, Canada shows an opposite distribution. Industrial activity dominates Canadian water usage at 80%, while domestic and agricultural sectors account for only modest shares, at approximately 10% each.","word_count":211,"revision_notes":[]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["概述地球水以咸水为主、淡水以冰川为主；埃及和沙特以农业用水为主，加拿大以工业为主。","先写水资源分布的两个饼图，再写三国用途的柱状图，避免把不同分母混合。","淡水占总水3%，冰川79%是淡水内部占比；无法精确读数时用 about/roughly。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"account for","meaning_zh":"占比例","usage":"accounted for X% of ..."},{"expression":"the corresponding figure","meaning_zh":"对应数值","usage":"the corresponding figure for ..."},{"expression":"percentage points","meaning_zh":"百分点","usage":"a gap of X percentage points"},{"expression":"respectively","meaning_zh":"分别","usage":"A and B were X and Y respectively"},{"expression":"the largest proportion","meaning_zh":"最大占比","usage":"recorded the largest proportion"},{"expression":"in comparison with","meaning_zh":"与之比较","usage":"in comparison with ..."}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9866&scene=%E9%9D%99%E6%80%81%E5%9B%BE&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9865","type":"writing","title":"政府部门女性领导","book":"密题范文-小作文","part":1,"description":"Task 1 · 至少 150 词","minWords":150,"prompt":"The table shows the position of women in governments and management in 2000 in 5 countries.\nSummarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.\nWrite at least 150 words.","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">The table shows the position of women in governments and management in 2000 in 5 countries.<br>Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.<br>Write at least 150 words.<br></div><p><img src=\"./assets/d5b8029b58917b25c98ceb214a239b2f8ae57b161726ef773e0d00361b763cc0.jpg\" width=\"1027\" height=\"486\" style=\"width: 1027px; height: 486px;\"/></p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website_with_ai_corrections","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"The table compares the proportions of women holding positions in government and management in five countries—Canada, Norway, Trinidad and Tobago, Uruguay, and Italy—in 2000.\nOverall, women accounted for considerably higher proportions of management positions than government positions in all five countries. Norway had the highest level of female representation in parliament, whereas Italy recorded the highest proportion in management, followed closely by Norway.\nIn terms of parliamentary representation, Norway ranked first, with women making up 38% of parliamentarians, followed by Canada at 28%. At the other end of the scale, Uruguay recorded the lowest figure, at just 8%, with Italy only slightly higher at 10%.\nTurning to management positions, the proportions were higher than that in parliament across all five countries. Italy had the highest figure, at 54%, followed by Norway at 52%, while Trinidad and Tobago stood at 40%. Canada and Uruguay recorded identical proportions of 37%. Notably, the proportion of female managers in Uruguay was almost five times that of female parliamentarians, despite the country having the lowest level of female parliamentary representation.","word_count":177,"revision_notes":["Italy and Norway jointly recorded the highest proportion in management → Italy recorded the highest proportion in management, followed closely by Norway","Italy and Norway shared the highest figure, at 54%, while Trinidad and Tobago stood at 45% → Italy had the highest figure, at 54%, followed by Norway at 52%, while Trinidad and Tobago stood at 40%"]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["概述五国女性管理职位占比均高于议会职位；挪威议会占比最高，意大利管理职位占比最高。","一段比较议会占比，另一段比较管理职位，补充乌拉圭两类职位差距。","按原图核对：挪威管理职位52%，意大利54%，特立尼达和多巴哥40%；不能写两国并列54%。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"account for","meaning_zh":"占比例","usage":"accounted for X% of ..."},{"expression":"the corresponding figure","meaning_zh":"对应数值","usage":"the corresponding figure for ..."},{"expression":"percentage points","meaning_zh":"百分点","usage":"a gap of X percentage points"},{"expression":"respectively","meaning_zh":"分别","usage":"A and B were X and Y respectively"},{"expression":"the largest proportion","meaning_zh":"最大占比","usage":"recorded the largest proportion"},{"expression":"in comparison with","meaning_zh":"与之比较","usage":"in comparison with ..."}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9865&scene=%E9%9D%99%E6%80%81%E5%9B%BE&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9864","type":"writing","title":"五国女性就业率","book":"密题范文-小作文","part":1,"description":"Task 1 · 至少 150 词","minWords":150,"prompt":"The line graph below gives information about the percentage of women aged 15-64 in employment between 2003 and 2009.\nSummarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.\nWrite at least 150 words.","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">The line graph below gives information about the percentage of women aged 15-64 in employment between 2003 and 2009.<br>Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.<br>Write at least 150 words.<br></div><p><img src=\"./assets/b513f2a65b1bd83f0c8e5c30f29d5379861f51cd732139da0dd229dfced594f4.png\" width=\"925\" height=\"722\" style=\"width: 925px; height: 722px;\"/></p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website_with_ai_corrections","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"The line graph compares the percentages of women aged 15 to 64 who were in employment in five countries in 2003, 2005, 2007 and 2009.\nOverall, Iceland recorded the highest employment rates throughout the period, while Turkey had the lowest. Germany and Chile experienced clear increases, whereas Canada remained largely stable. Iceland and Turkey were also the only two countries to show an overall decline.\nIceland's figure remained unchanged at 81% from 2003 to 2007, before falling slightly to 78% in 2009. In contrast, Turkey started at just 25% and dropped to 21% in 2005, after which it gradually recovered. Despite this recovery, its rate was still marginally lower in 2009 than in 2003.\nAmong the other three countries, Germany saw the most notable growth, with the proportion of employed women rising steadily from 58% to 65% over the period. Chile followed a similar upward trend, increasing from 35% to 41%. Canada, however, experienced very little change, with its figure remaining close to 70% throughout.","word_count":165,"revision_notes":["The table compares → The line graph compares"]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["概述冰岛始终最高、土耳其最低；德国和智利上升，加拿大较稳定。","高低两组分段，写冰岛后期下降、土耳其先降后回升，以及德国和智利的持续增长。","原图是折线图；描述15至64岁女性中的就业百分比，不能写成就业人数。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"rise steadily","meaning_zh":"稳步上升","usage":"rose steadily from A to B"},{"expression":"reach a peak","meaning_zh":"达到峰值","usage":"reached a peak of X"},{"expression":"remain stable","meaning_zh":"保持稳定","usage":"remained stable at X"},{"expression":"fluctuate","meaning_zh":"波动","usage":"fluctuated between A and B"},{"expression":"recover","meaning_zh":"回升","usage":"recovered to X"},{"expression":"by contrast","meaning_zh":"相比之下","usage":"By contrast, the figure for ..."}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9864&scene=%E5%8A%A8%E6%80%81%E5%9B%BE&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9860","type":"writing","title":"澳大利亚学生宿舍","book":"密题范文-小作文","part":1,"description":"Task 1 · 至少 150 词","minWords":150,"prompt":"The plans below show a student room for two people and a student room for one person at an Australian university.\nSummarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.\nWrite at least 150 words.","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">The plans below show a student room for two people and a student room for one person at an Australian university.<br>Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.<br>Write at least 150 words.<br></div><p><img src=\"./assets/a44d234cf495bd2349bc200fed8083fd85f20ee52bed41380206c7f91a50b344.jpg\" width=\"885\" height=\"863\" style=\"width: 885px; height: 863px;\"/></p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website_with_ai_corrections","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"The plans compare two types of student accommodation at an Australian university: a room for two people and a room for one person.\n\nOverall, the double room is wider and has a higher weekly rent, as well as providing more furniture. Both rooms are six metres long and include a bathroom, study space and cooking facilities.\n\nThe room for two students measures four metres in width and costs $350 per week. The single room is only 2.5 metres wide and has a weekly rent of $200. In both layouts, the bathroom is located at the upper left of the plan, while the beds are positioned on the right beside windows.\n\nThe double room contains two beds and two study desks, with cupboards separating the two sleeping areas. It also has a table and chairs, which are absent from the single room. A bookshelf is shown near the bathroom in each layout. The double room's stove, sink and microwave are arranged along the left side, whereas the same appliances are grouped along the lower left side of the single room. Each room also includes a television.","word_count":185,"revision_notes":["AI依据原图重写布局描述，使用图中相对位置并核对家具。"]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["概述双人房更宽、总周租更高，家具与设施更多；两类房间长度相同。","先比较尺寸与租金，再按图中位置说明床、书桌、浴室、厨房及储物设施。","用左侧、右侧等相对位置，图无指南针时不假定方位；图中$350标价是整间双人房的周租。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"floor plan","meaning_zh":"平面图","usage":"The floor plans compare ..."},{"expression":"be located next to","meaning_zh":"位于旁边","usage":"is located next to the bathroom"},{"expression":"shared facilities","meaning_zh":"共用设施","usage":"a room with shared facilities"},{"expression":"in width","meaning_zh":"宽度上","usage":"measures four metres in width"},{"expression":"weekly rent","meaning_zh":"周租","usage":"a weekly rent of ..."},{"expression":"be equipped with","meaning_zh":"配备","usage":"is equipped with two desks"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9860&scene=%E9%9D%99%E6%80%81%E5%9B%BE&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9859","type":"writing","title":"各国名校数量","book":"密题范文-小作文","part":1,"description":"Task 1 · 至少 150 词","minWords":150,"prompt":"The table shows the number of universities ranked top 200 in the world (2011) in three subjects in five countries.\nSummarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.\nWrite at least 150 words.","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">The table shows the number of universities ranked top 200 in the world (2011) in three subjects in five countries.<br>Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.<br>Write at least 150 words.<br></div><p><img src=\"./assets/dbbd49d23ac779ffe5acc6ca9e30c9ec82605abba8b8c76ff50321a28fb33997.png\" width=\"1143\" height=\"565\" style=\"width: 1143px; height: 565px;\"/></p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"The table details the number of top-200 universities in five countries across three subjects—Biology, Medicine, and Psychology—in the year 2011.\nOverall, the USA was the dominant leader across all three disciplines by a substantial margin, followed by the United Kingdom. In contrast, New Zealand accounted for the lowest numbers. Additionally, Biology and Psychology generally featured a higher number of top-ranked institutions than Medicine in most countries.\nLooking at the two highest-ranking nations, the USA stood out with 69 institutions in Biology, 58 in Psychology, and 54 in Medicine. The UK followed a very similar structural pattern, though at lower volumes, recording 30 top universities in Biology, 29 in Psychology, and 24 in Medicine.\nAmong the remaining countries, Australia and Canada exhibited near-identical patterns, both having their highest number of top universities in Psychology (17 and 14, respectively), followed by Medicine and Biology (9 each). Conversely, New Zealand registered the lowest figures across all categories.","word_count":156,"revision_notes":[]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["概述美国在三个学科均领先，英国第二，新西兰数量最少。","先比较美国和英国，再比较澳大利亚、加拿大、新西兰；补充各国内的学科高低。","单位为进入全球前200的大学数量，不是学生数、国家总大学数或整体综合排名。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"ranked among the top 200","meaning_zh":"排名进入前200","usage":"universities ranked among the top 200"},{"expression":"the highest number","meaning_zh":"数量最多","usage":"recorded the highest number"},{"expression":"academic discipline","meaning_zh":"学科","usage":"across three academic disciplines"},{"expression":"institution","meaning_zh":"院校","usage":"top-ranked institutions"},{"expression":"by a substantial margin","meaning_zh":"以较大差距","usage":"led by a substantial margin"},{"expression":"respectively","meaning_zh":"分别","usage":"A and B recorded X and Y respectively"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9859&scene=%E9%9D%99%E6%80%81%E5%9B%BE&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9826","type":"writing","title":"澳洲某大学六系学生情况 ","book":"密题范文-小作文","part":1,"description":"Task 1 · 至少 150 词","minWords":150,"prompt":"The table below gives information about students studying in six departments in an Australian university in 2009.\nSummarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">The table below gives information about students studying in six departments in an Australian university in 2009.<br>Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.<br></div><p><img src=\"./assets/f1fab77b1c3ab1554394d68576599e589e77f168e57f681c23caf5b606af6eae.png\" width=\"1008\" height=\"648\" style=\"width: 1008px; height: 648px;\"/></p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"The table compares the percentages of students who were female, whose language was not English, and who were born outside Australia in six departments at an Australian university in 2009.\nOverall, female students were considerably better represented in the humanities and language-related departments than in the science subjects. In addition, the proportion of students born outside Australia was higher than that of students whose language was not English in every department.\nIn terms of gender, females accounted for 67% of students in English, followed by 63% in Modern Languages and 58% in History. By contrast, their proportions were substantially lower in the three science departments, at 42% in Mathematics, 37% in Physics and just 29% in Chemistry. Thus, the gap between the highest and lowest figures was 38 percentage points.\nA similar pattern can be seen in the other two categories. Modern Languages had the largest proportions of students whose language was not English and those born outside Australia, at 41% and 54%, respectively. At the other end of the scale, History had the lowest figures, at 10% and 18%. Among the science departments, Physics had the highest proportion of non-English-language students, at 38%, while Chemistry had the largest percentage of overseas-born students, at 47%. In all six departments, the percentage of overseas-born students exceeded the corresponding figure for those whose language was not English.","word_count":225,"revision_notes":[]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["概述语言与人文学科女性占比较高；所有系的海外出生者占比均高于第一语言非英语者。","一段按性别比较文理系，另一段比较语言与出生地两类数据，突出极值。","三列统计口径独立，不能相加求总数；第一语言非英语不等于英语能力不足。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"account for","meaning_zh":"占比例","usage":"accounted for X% of ..."},{"expression":"the corresponding figure","meaning_zh":"对应数值","usage":"the corresponding figure for ..."},{"expression":"percentage points","meaning_zh":"百分点","usage":"a gap of X percentage points"},{"expression":"respectively","meaning_zh":"分别","usage":"A and B were X and Y respectively"},{"expression":"the largest proportion","meaning_zh":"最大占比","usage":"recorded the largest proportion"},{"expression":"in comparison with","meaning_zh":"与之比较","usage":"in comparison with ..."}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9826&scene=%E9%9D%99%E6%80%81%E5%9B%BE&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9823","type":"writing","title":"音乐公司销量","book":"密题范文-小作文","part":1,"description":"Task 1 · 至少 150 词","minWords":150,"prompt":"The pie charts below show the percentage of total music sales shared among different music companies in the years 1997, 2002 and 2007.\nSummarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.\nWrite at least 150 words.","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">The pie charts below show the percentage of total music sales shared among different music companies in the years 1997, 2002 and 2007.<br>Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.<br>Write at least 150 words.<br></div><p><img src=\"./assets/6234130e8f3a16fceda6a514ada37b30e4c0ef71c92bb2beb8a44ca2dabb90dc.png\" width=\"594\" height=\"904\" style=\"width: 594px; height: 904px;\"/></p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website_with_ai_corrections","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"The pie charts illustrate the distribution of music sales among five companies in 1997, 2002, and 2007.\nOverall, Kran and Bec grew to dominate the market by 2007. Conversely, Telco’s recorded share fell to zero, while the share for \"Others\" shrank continuously. Goz was the only entity that remained entirely unchanged.\nIn 1997, Kran held the largest market share at 35%, followed by Telco and Others at 20% each. Bec and Goz accounted for smaller portions at 15% and 10% respectively. By 2002, Kran extended its lead to 40%, while Bec expanded rapidly to 25%. In contrast, Telco’s share fell to 15%, and Others was halved to 10%, tying with Goz, which stayed constant.\nBy 2007, Kran reached a peak of 55%, capturing over half of total sales. Bec also continued its upward trend to hit 30%, meaning these top two companies together controlled 85% of the market. On the other hand, Telco’s share fell to 0%. The percentage for Others diminished further to a minimal 5%, whereas Goz retained its steady 10% share.","word_count":174,"revision_notes":["Telco experienced a total collapse → Telco’s recorded share fell to zero","Telco completely exited the market at 0% → Telco’s share fell to 0%"]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["概述Kran与Bec份额扩大、Telco降至零、Goz稳定；Others逐渐缩小。","按1997、2002、2007展开，或将上升企业和下降企业分组，并提供代表性数据。","只说明市场份额变化；份额为零不能单凭图表断言公司倒闭或市场总销量下跌。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"account for","meaning_zh":"占比例","usage":"accounted for X% of ..."},{"expression":"the corresponding figure","meaning_zh":"对应数值","usage":"the corresponding figure for ..."},{"expression":"percentage points","meaning_zh":"百分点","usage":"a gap of X percentage points"},{"expression":"respectively","meaning_zh":"分别","usage":"A and B were X and Y respectively"},{"expression":"the largest proportion","meaning_zh":"最大占比","usage":"recorded the largest proportion"},{"expression":"in comparison with","meaning_zh":"与之比较","usage":"in comparison with ..."}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9823&scene=%E5%8A%A8%E6%80%81%E5%9B%BE&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9822","type":"writing","title":"欧盟失业率变化","book":"密题范文-小作文","part":1,"description":"Task 1 · 至少 150 词","minWords":150,"prompt":"The graph below compares the percentage of unemployed workers in the European Union (all workers) with the percentages in the three categories, Professional, Manual and Self-employed.\nSummarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.\nWrite at least 150 words.","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">The graph below compares the percentage of unemployed workers in the European Union (all workers) with the percentages in the three categories, Professional, Manual and Self-employed.<br>Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.<br>Write at least 150 words.<br></div><p><img src=\"./assets/859f5a68075c897e4d3b6b8bcafd3c8e48961cab2e4c88c7d009ea6b876c9c65.png\" width=\"888\" height=\"717\" style=\"width: 888px; height: 717px;\"/></p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website_with_ai_corrections","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"The line graph compares the unemployment rates among all workers and three specific occupational categories in the European Union between 1990 and 1999.\nOverall, the unemployment rate for all workers increased over the decade, as did the rates for manual and self-employed workers. The professional rate fluctuated but ended close to its initial level. Notably, manual workers initially suffered the highest jobless rates, but were eventually overtaken by self-employed workers, while professional workers consistently recorded the lowest figures.\nIn 1990, manual workers had the highest unemployment rate at around 7%, followed by the self-employed (6%), all workers (5%), and professional workers (2%). Over the next few years, figures for all categories rose. Manual worker unemployment peaked at just over 14% in 1994 before falling steeply, while self-employed rates climbed steadily, reaching a high plateau of about 12.5% from 1996 to 1999.\nUnemployment for all workers and professionals both peaked in 1997 at approximately 12.5% and 5.5%, respectively. By 1999, self-employed workers became the most affected group at 12.5%. Meanwhile, rates for all workers and manual workers dropped to around 10.1% and 9.7%, whereas professional unemployment returned to its starting level of roughly 2%.","word_count":193,"revision_notes":["Overall, unemployment rates for all groups experienced upward trends with fluctuations over the decade. → Overall, the unemployment rate for all workers increased over the decade, as did the rates for manual and self-employed workers. The professional rate fluctuated but ended close to its initial level.","were eventually overtook → were eventually overtaken"]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["概述总体失业率上升后回落；专业人员一直较低，体力劳动者波动较大。","把总体与自雇人员放一组，专业人员与体力劳动者放另一组；标出不同峰值年份。","区分 overall unemployment 和各类工人的 unemployment rate，读清四种线型。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"rise steadily","meaning_zh":"稳步上升","usage":"rose steadily from A to B"},{"expression":"reach a peak","meaning_zh":"达到峰值","usage":"reached a peak of X"},{"expression":"remain stable","meaning_zh":"保持稳定","usage":"remained stable at X"},{"expression":"fluctuate","meaning_zh":"波动","usage":"fluctuated between A and B"},{"expression":"recover","meaning_zh":"回升","usage":"recovered to X"},{"expression":"by contrast","meaning_zh":"相比之下","usage":"By contrast, the figure for ..."}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9822&scene=%E5%8A%A8%E6%80%81%E5%9B%BE&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9820","type":"writing","title":"男性的平均身高","book":"密题范文-小作文","part":1,"description":"Task 1 · 至少 150 词","minWords":150,"prompt":"The line graph illustrates the average height of men in four countries (Denmark, the USA, Great Britain and France) over the period from 1775 to 1975.\nSummarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.\nWrite at least 150 words.","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">The line graph illustrates the average height of men in four countries (Denmark, the USA, Great Britain and France) over the period from 1775 to 1975.<br>Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.<br>Write at least 150 words.<br></div><p><img src=\"./assets/992225bc336de85dd23fba0840111e06f0694f4125c17f0b3fca88738647a106.jpg\" width=\"1208\" height=\"741\" style=\"width: 1208px; height: 741px;\"/></p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website_with_ai_corrections","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"The line graph compares the average height of adult males in Denmark, the USA, Great Britain, and France from 1775 to 1975.\nOverall, male heights in all four nations fluctuated during the first century before undergoing a dramatic, sustained increase after 1875.\nIn 1775, the USA led at around 167 cm, closely followed by Great Britain at 166 cm. Despite peaking at roughly 171 cm early in the period, American height fell to 165 cm by 1875, matching British men. Meanwhile, Denmark’s figure hovered between 160 cm and 163 cm before settling at 161 cm in 1875. French men were generally among the shortest, fluctuating around 160 cm throughout this period.\nFrom 1875 onwards, all countries experienced a distinct upward trend. Denmark saw the most extraordinary rise, surging from 161 cm to approximately 186 cm in 1975 to surpass all other nations. Concurrently, the figures for both the USA and Great Britain climbed steadily to reach around 181 cm. Although French men also grew taller, reaching roughly 174 cm by 1975, France remained the lowest throughout the final century.","word_count":179,"revision_notes":["mid-century → early in the period","French men remained the shortest, → French men were generally among the shortest,"]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["概述四国身高前期波动、1875年后明显上升；丹麦后期增幅最大、末期最高。","先比较1775年至1875年的较小波动，再比较此后上升幅度；法国末期仍最低，美国和英国末期接近。","单位为厘米，使用 approximate values；不能根据身高曲线推断人口或营养原因。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"average height","meaning_zh":"平均身高","usage":"the average height of adult males"},{"expression":"rise steadily","meaning_zh":"稳步上升","usage":"rose steadily to X centimetres"},{"expression":"fluctuate","meaning_zh":"波动","usage":"fluctuated around X centimetres"},{"expression":"surpass","meaning_zh":"超过","usage":"surpassed the other countries"},{"expression":"upward trend","meaning_zh":"上升趋势","usage":"experienced an upward trend"},{"expression":"approximately","meaning_zh":"大约","usage":"approximately X centimetres"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9820&scene=%E5%8A%A8%E6%80%81%E5%9B%BE&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9818","type":"writing","title":"剧院评价","book":"密题范文-小作文","part":1,"description":"Task 1 · 至少 150 词","minWords":150,"prompt":"The charts below show response to a questionnaire given by two groups of people (Club members and the general public) who showed their opinions about a new theatre.\nSummarise the information by selecting and reporting the mainfeatures, and make comparisons where relevant.","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">The charts below show response to a questionnaire given by two groups of people (Club members and the general public) who showed their opinions about a new theatre.<br>Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the mainfeatures, and make comparisons where relevant.<br></div><p><img src=\"./assets/5146f2c79b6079691ab94b093180684a182b165793404353a1d8f0f1e582958c.png\"/></p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"The tables compare feedback from club members and the general public on three features of a new theatre: facilities, information, and quality.\nOverall, both groups held positive views, with the vast majority rating every aspect as excellent or satisfied. Club members were most impressed with quality and facilities, whereas the public awarded higher marks to information.\nRegarding facilities, 72% of club members rated them \"Excellent,\" slightly above the public's 64%. Satisfaction stood at 26% and 24% respectively, while only a small minority in both groups rated them as poor (2% and 8%).\nIn terms of quality, club members were exceptionally positive, with 88% choosing \"Excellent\" compared to 53% of the public. Conversely, 40% of the public felt satisfied, four times higher than the club members' 10%.\nFinally, for information, the trend reversed. The public gave higher praise, with 68% rating it \"Excellent\" versus 54% of club members. Meanwhile, 16% of club members gave a \"Poor\" rating, the highest negative response recorded across all categories.","word_count":164,"revision_notes":[]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["概述两个群体总体评价积极，会员对设施和质量更满意，公众对信息更满意。","按设施、质量、信息分组比较会员与公众，突出质量评价的35个百分点差异。","群体是俱乐部会员与普通公众，不是男女；各表的三类评价以本群体受访者为分母。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"account for","meaning_zh":"占比例","usage":"accounted for X% of ..."},{"expression":"the corresponding figure","meaning_zh":"对应数值","usage":"the corresponding figure for ..."},{"expression":"percentage points","meaning_zh":"百分点","usage":"a gap of X percentage points"},{"expression":"respectively","meaning_zh":"分别","usage":"A and B were X and Y respectively"},{"expression":"the largest proportion","meaning_zh":"最大占比","usage":"recorded the largest proportion"},{"expression":"in comparison with","meaning_zh":"与之比较","usage":"in comparison with ..."}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9818&scene=%E9%9D%99%E6%80%81%E5%9B%BE&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9817","type":"writing","title":"政府开支","book":"密题范文-小作文","part":1,"description":"Task 1 · 至少 150 词","minWords":150,"prompt":"The table below shows the percentage of government spending on education and training and the participation of 18–24 year-olds in education and training in five countries in 2012.\nSummarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">The table below shows the percentage of government spending on education and training and the participation of 18–24 year-olds in education and training in five countries in 2012.<br>Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.<br></div><p><img src=\"./assets/3e83585a687dd15de0259a241a87390bb1052124a79a43c24e5634f0fc32dd62.png\" width=\"1077\" height=\"623\" style=\"width: 1077px; height: 623px;\"/></p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"The table compares five European nations in terms of the proportion of government spending allocated to education and training, together with the share of 18–24-year-olds taking part in such programmes in 2012.\nOverall, Slovenia invested the highest percentage of public funds in education and training, while Poland recorded the lowest figure. It is notable that Poland achieved the greatest participation rate among young adults even with the lowest level of government spending.\nIn terms of government investment, Slovenia spent 25% of its budget on education and training, far above the figure for Hungary (13%). Romania and the Czech Republic spent 10% and 9% respectively, while Poland’s share of expenditure was only 5%, the lowest among the five countries.\nWhen it comes to youth participation, Poland had the highest proportion at 44%. Slovenia followed with 40%, ahead of Hungary at 34%. By contrast, fewer young people took part in education and training in the Czech Republic (27%) and Romania, where the participation rate stood at just 23%.","word_count":167,"revision_notes":[]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["概述斯洛文尼亚教育培训支出占比最高，波兰最低；青年参与率却是波兰最高。","先按国家比较支出占比，再比较18至24岁青年参与率，突出两种排序并不一致。","支出占政府预算的比例与青年参与率是不同分母，不能据此证明高投入必然提高参与率。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"account for","meaning_zh":"占比例","usage":"accounted for X% of ..."},{"expression":"the corresponding figure","meaning_zh":"对应数值","usage":"the corresponding figure for ..."},{"expression":"percentage points","meaning_zh":"百分点","usage":"a gap of X percentage points"},{"expression":"respectively","meaning_zh":"分别","usage":"A and B were X and Y respectively"},{"expression":"the largest proportion","meaning_zh":"最大占比","usage":"recorded the largest proportion"},{"expression":"in comparison with","meaning_zh":"与之比较","usage":"in comparison with ..."}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9817&scene=%E9%9D%99%E6%80%81%E5%9B%BE&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9232","type":"writing","title":"Task2 高中毕业后间隔年的利弊","book":"邪21","part":2,"description":"Task 2 · 至少 250 词","minWords":250,"prompt":"Some students choose to work or travel after leaving school and before going to university. Many people, however, say that working experience is more useful in adult life than traveling.\nDo you agree or disagree with this statement?","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">Some students choose to work or travel after leaving school and before going to university. Many people, however, say that working experience is more useful in adult life than traveling.<br>Do you agree or disagree with this statement?<br>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.<br>Write at least 250 words.</div><p>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.</p><p><br/></p><p><br/></p><p>Write at least 250 words.</p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"In recent years, an increasing number of students have chosen to work or travel after finishing school but before enrolling in university. While both options offer benefits, I believe that gaining work experience provides more long-term value and practical skills that are essential for adult life.\nFirstly, working before university helps students develop vital skills that are highly sought after in today's job market, such as communication, time management, and teamwork. For example, jobs like customer service teach patience, conflict resolution, and problem-solving, while internships offer industry-specific experience that gives students a clear understanding of their future career paths. This hands-on experience makes students more employable and allows them to make informed choices about their studies and career ambitions.\nIn addition to skill development, working provides financial independence, which can greatly ease the transition to university life. Students who work can save money for their education, reducing the burden of tuition fees and living expenses. This financial stability also fosters responsibility, teaching budgeting and financial planning, which are essential skills in adulthood. These early lessons in managing personal finances prepare students for the financial realities they will face in the future.\nWhile traveling can be a valuable and enriching experience, its direct benefits for adult life are often less tangible. Traveling exposes students to new cultures and enhances personal growth, but these experiences may not be as immediately applicable in the workplace as the practical skills gained through work. Although travel can foster adaptability and independence, these qualities are generally less relevant in professional settings compared to the hard skills developed through employment.\nIn conclusion, although traveling offers cultural enrichment, work experience provides more practical and long-lasting benefits. It equips students with crucial skills, financial responsibility, and career clarity, making it a more advantageous choice for preparing for adult life and future success.","word_count":303,"revision_notes":[]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["本题不是笼统讨论间隔年利弊，而是比较工作与旅行哪种经历对成年生活更有用。先明确赞同程度。","主体一写工作培养沟通、预算与职业技能；主体二承认旅行培养适应力与文化理解，再说明为何工作更直接有用，或提出相反立场。","每段都回到成年生活的实用性，不仅列出两种活动的好处。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"gap year","meaning_zh":"间隔年","usage":""},{"expression":"financial independence","meaning_zh":"经济独立","usage":""},{"expression":"practical experience","meaning_zh":"实践经验","usage":""},{"expression":"academic motivation","meaning_zh":"学习动力","usage":""},{"expression":"career direction","meaning_zh":"职业方向","usage":""},{"expression":"resume formal education","meaning_zh":"恢复正规学习","usage":""}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9232&scene=%E6%95%99%E8%82%B2&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9234","type":"writing","title":"Task2 垃圾食品","book":"邪21","part":2,"description":"Task 2 · 至少 250 词","minWords":250,"prompt":"Some people claim that school should educate children about the effects of junk food on their health while others claim that education about this starts at home.\nDiscuss both sides and give your opinion.","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">Some people claim that school should educate children about the effects of junk food on their health while others claim that education about this starts at home.<br>Discuss both sides and give your opinion.<br>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.<br>Write at least 250 words.</div><p style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.&nbsp;</span></p><p style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><br/></p><p style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Write at least 250 words.</span></p><p><br/></p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"There is ongoing debate about whether schools or parents should take responsibility for educating children about the health risks of junk food. While some argue that this education belongs in the classroom, others believe it should begin at home. In my view, both play crucial roles, but schools have a unique opportunity to reinforce healthy habits systematically.\nOn one hand, parents are the primary influencers in a child’s early years. Eating habits often develop at home, where parents control meal choices and model behaviors. For example, if parents consistently choose nutritious snacks over processed foods, children are more likely to adopt similar preferences. Moreover, discussions about food can be personalized at home—parents can address their child’s specific tastes or dietary restrictions, such as allergies or specific health needs. This individualized approach helps children understand the direct impact of junk food on their well-being.\nOn the other hand, schools provide structured education to all children, ensuring no one misses critical health lessons. Many students consume meals at school, making it an ideal setting to teach balanced eating. For instance, schools can integrate nutrition into science classes, demonstrate healthy cooking in home economics, or even ban junk food in cafeterias. Peer influence also matters—when children learn together, they encourage each other to make better choices. Without school-based education, students from less health-conscious families might remain unaware of junk food’s dangers, such as obesity or diabetes.\nIn conclusion, while parents lay the foundation for healthy habits, schools must amplify this education to reach all children equally. A collaborative approach—where parents model good practices and schools provide evidence-based knowledge—would most effectively combat the junk food epidemic.","word_count":276,"revision_notes":[]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["讨论学校与家庭谁应教育儿童了解垃圾食品影响，并给出个人观点。","家庭通过日常饮食示范和个别指导建立习惯；学校通过系统课程、公平覆盖和校园餐食强化知识。","可支持共同承担，但说明分工。不要将文章写成是否禁止垃圾食品。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"nutrition education","meaning_zh":"营养教育","usage":""},{"expression":"parental influence","meaning_zh":"家长影响","usage":""},{"expression":"healthy eating habits","meaning_zh":"健康饮食习惯","usage":""},{"expression":"school-based programmes","meaning_zh":"以学校为基础的课程","usage":""},{"expression":"balanced diet","meaning_zh":"均衡饮食","usage":""},{"expression":"shared responsibility","meaning_zh":"共同责任","usage":""}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9234&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E7%94%9F%E6%B4%BB&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9236","type":"writing","title":"Task2 努力决心vs 金钱外表","book":"邪21","part":2,"description":"Task 2 · 至少 250 词","minWords":250,"prompt":"Some people believe that hard work and determination are key factors for success, while others argue that money and personal appearance are more important.\nDiscuss both views and give your opinion.","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">Some people believe that hard work and determination are key factors for success, while others argue that money and personal appearance are more important.<br>Discuss both views and give your opinion.<br>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.<br>Write at least 250 words.</div><p>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Write at least 250 words.</p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"People have different opinions about what contributes most to success. While some believe that hard work and determination are essential, others argue that financial advantages and personal appearance play a more important role. Both perspectives have merit, and this essay will examine them before offering my own view.\nThose who emphasise hard work and determination point out that these qualities allow individuals to overcome difficulties and achieve long-term goals. Many successful people, particularly entrepreneurs and athletes, attribute their achievements to perseverance despite repeated failures. Hard work also enables people to acquire new skills and improve their performance, which increases their chances of success regardless of their background. Moreover, determination often leads to discipline and patience, two qualities that are widely recognised as foundations for lasting achievement.\nOn the other hand, some argue that money and appearance can provide significant advantages. Wealth gives people access to better education, more resources and valuable social connections. For example, a person from a wealthy family may be able to attend prestigious schools or invest in business opportunities that are unavailable to others. Personal appearance can also play a role in certain fields, such as entertainment, media or sales, where first impressions and visual appeal strongly influence people’s decisions. From this viewpoint, financial and physical advantages can open doors that hard work alone may not.\nIn my opinion, although money and appearance can offer some benefits, they are not as important as hard work and determination in the long run. While financial support may create opportunities, success ultimately depends on a person’s ability to take advantage of those opportunities, which requires effort and persistence. Likewise, appearance may help someone in the early stages of their career, but it cannot sustain long-term success without real ability and commitment. Hard-working individuals are more likely to adapt to challenges, continue improving and achieve stable success.","word_count":307,"revision_notes":[]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["比较努力与决心带来的持续进步，以及金钱和外貌提供的初始机会。","一段解释练习和坚持如何提升能力；另一段承认资源与形象的作用，并限定适用行业。","观点可为努力更关键但资源仍重要；避免声称成功完全由某单一因素决定。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"determination","meaning_zh":"决心","usage":""},{"expression":"perseverance","meaning_zh":"坚持","usage":""},{"expression":"financial resources","meaning_zh":"财力资源","usage":""},{"expression":"initial advantage","meaning_zh":"初始优势","usage":""},{"expression":"professional competence","meaning_zh":"职业能力","usage":""},{"expression":"long-term achievement","meaning_zh":"长期成就","usage":""}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9236&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E7%94%9F%E6%B4%BB&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9238","type":"writing","title":"Task2 生育年龄推迟","book":"邪21","part":2,"description":"Task 2 · 至少 250 词","minWords":250,"prompt":"Some people choose to have their first child at an older age.\nWhat are the reasons?\nDo the advantages outweigh the disadvantages?","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">Some people choose to have their first child at an older age.<br>What are the reasons?<br>Do the advantages outweigh the disadvantages?<br>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.<br>Write at least 250 words.</div><p>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Write at least 250 words.</p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"In many countries today, an increasing number of people choose to have their first child at a later age. This trend is influenced by several social and economic factors. Although delaying parenthood has both advantages and disadvantages, I believe the benefits generally outweigh the drawbacks.\nOne major reason why people become parents later is the desire to establish a stable career before starting a family. In modern society, many young adults focus on higher education and professional development in their twenties. They hope to secure a well-paid job, gain financial independence, and create a comfortable living environment before welcoming a child. Another contributing factor is the high cost of raising children. Housing, childcare, and education expenses have risen sharply in recent years, making younger couples feel unprepared to take on the financial burden. In addition, many people now value personal growth and prefer to spend their early adulthood travelling, exploring hobbies, or building relationships, which naturally delays parenthood.\nDespite some clear disadvantages, such as reduced fertility and increased health risks during pregnancy, having children later in life also offers significant benefits. Older parents are usually more emotionally mature and better prepared to take on the responsibilities of raising a child. They tend to have greater financial stability, which allows them to provide a safer home, better healthcare, and more educational opportunities for their children. Moreover, parents who have already achieved personal and professional goals may feel less pressure balancing work and family, allowing them to spend more quality time with their child. In contrast, very young parents often struggle with stress, limited income, and lack of life experience, which can affect both their well-being and their child’s development.\nIn conclusion, people choose to have their first child later for financial, educational, and personal reasons. Although this trend can create some challenges, I believe that the advantages, particularly greater stability and maturity, outweigh the disadvantages for most families.","word_count":317,"revision_notes":[]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["同时回答晚育原因和利弊是否相抵，不能只讨论优缺点。","原因可写职业与育儿成本；收益写经济稳定和成熟度，风险写健康与精力。","明确比较两方影响；按不同家庭条件展开，举例说明稳定收入与育儿准备如何影响权衡。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"delayed parenthood","meaning_zh":"晚育","usage":""},{"expression":"financial stability","meaning_zh":"经济稳定","usage":""},{"expression":"emotional maturity","meaning_zh":"情感成熟","usage":""},{"expression":"childcare costs","meaning_zh":"育儿费用","usage":""},{"expression":"career development","meaning_zh":"职业发展","usage":""},{"expression":"family responsibilities","meaning_zh":"家庭责任","usage":""}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9238&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E7%94%9F%E6%B4%BB&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9870","type":"writing","title":"环保靠政府还是个人","book":"密题范文-大作文","part":2,"description":"Task 2 · 至少 250 词","minWords":250,"prompt":"Reducing global environmental damage should be handled by governments rather than individuals.\nTo what extent do you agree or disagree?","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">Reducing global environmental damage should be handled by governments rather than individuals.<br>To what extent do you agree or disagree?<br>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.<br>Write at least 250 words.</div><p>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.</p><p><br/></p><p>Write at least 250 words.</p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"Environmental degradation is accelerating at an alarming rate, primarily due to human activities. While some argue that mitigating this issue should be handled solely by governments rather than individuals, I strongly disagree. I believe that although governments must lead the charge through regulation and infrastructure, individual action is equally indispensable in combating global environmental damage.\nTo begin with, private transportation is a major contributor to global carbon emissions. If individuals make a conscious effort to alter their daily habits by reducing private car reliance and utilizing public transport, fossil fuel consumption will be substantially reduced. In other words, when commuters choose to travel regularly by buses or trains—which are often affordable and widespread—vehicle emissions drop significantly. However, this individual shift in mindset must be supported by governments providing efficient, clean, and accessible public transit systems, demonstrating that personal choices and state initiatives are mutually reinforcing.\nIn addition, individuals can play a vital role in safeguarding the environment by curbing their usage of single-use plastics, which are severe pollutants to soil and oceans. Currently, many consumers rely heavily on plastic bags while shopping, fostering a wasteful throwaway culture. To counteract this, personal efforts can be made by adopting eco-friendly substitutes, such as bringing reusable cloth bags to supermarkets. Furthermore, when individuals support green alternatives, it reinforces governmental plastic bans and encourages industries to adopt sustainable packaging.\nIn conclusion, global environmental issues are a pressing crisis that cannot be resolved through a single channel. While governments hold the power to pass laws and build green infrastructure, these policies remain ineffective without the active participation of the public. Therefore, individuals must work hand in hand with governments to ensure sustainable environmental protection.","word_count":281,"revision_notes":[]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["分别讨论政府与个人对环保的作用，再提出二者互补的立场。","政府能制定法规和投资基础设施；个人能减少浪费并通过消费形成需求。","用垃圾分类为例说明制度与行为如何配合，不仅罗列环保口号。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"environmental protection","meaning_zh":"环境保护","usage":""},{"expression":"individual responsibility","meaning_zh":"个人责任","usage":""},{"expression":"government regulation","meaning_zh":"政府监管","usage":""},{"expression":"public infrastructure","meaning_zh":"公共基础设施","usage":""},{"expression":"sustainable consumption","meaning_zh":"可持续消费","usage":""},{"expression":"collective action","meaning_zh":"集体行动","usage":""}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9870&scene=%E7%8E%AF%E5%A2%83&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9869","type":"writing","title":"太空旅行","book":"密题范文-大作文","part":2,"description":"Task 2 · 至少 250 词","minWords":250,"prompt":"Space travel has been possible for some time and some people believe that space tourism could be developed in the future.\nDo you think this would be a positive or negative development?","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">Space travel has been possible for some time and some people believe that space tourism could be developed in the future.<br>Do you think this would be a positive or negative development?<br>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.<br>Write at least 250 words.</div><p>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Write at least 250 words.</p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"In recent decades, significant advancements in science and technology have made space travel increasingly feasible, raising the prospect of widespread space tourism. Personally, I contend that this is a negative development due to the severe environmental risks it entails and the social inequalities it exacerbates.\nOn the one hand, proponents argue that commercial space tourism offers substantial economic and technological benefits. Private investment in the space tourism industry accelerates innovation in aerospace engineering, which can eventually yield practical applications for everyday society. For instance, breakthroughs in reusable rocket technology and lightweight composite materials—catalyzed by commercial space flights—hold the potential to revolutionize conventional aviation and global logistics. Additionally, the industry creates high-skilled jobs and stimulates local economies, particularly in regions hosting spaceports and specialized supply chains.\nOn the other hand, I firmly believe that space tourism represents an adverse trend due to the profound environmental and ethical concerns it raises. From an environmental perspective, rocket launches release large amounts of black carbon directly into the stratosphere, damaging the ozone layer and worsening global climate volatility—impacts that are currently unsustainable and difficult to mitigate. Socially, the enormous capital required for space tourism represents a critical misallocation of global resources. Prioritizing exorbitant joyrides for the ultra-rich while diverting funding away from pressing human crises, such as poverty alleviation, healthcare, and food security, only serves to deepen existing societal divides.\nIn conclusion, although space tourism may offer certain technological spillovers and economic opportunities, its disproportionate environmental toll and the social inequities it reinforces render it an overall negative development.","word_count":258,"revision_notes":[]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["按原题问法评价太空旅行的发展，区分科学探索与商业旅游。","支持理由可写技术创新和探索；反对理由可写成本、资源优先级及环境影响。","若立场有条件支持，明确公共收益与安全条件，避免杜撰研究结果。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"space exploration","meaning_zh":"太空探索","usage":""},{"expression":"commercial space travel","meaning_zh":"商业太空旅行","usage":""},{"expression":"technological innovation","meaning_zh":"技术创新","usage":""},{"expression":"public expenditure","meaning_zh":"公共支出","usage":""},{"expression":"environmental impact","meaning_zh":"环境影响","usage":""},{"expression":"safety standards","meaning_zh":"安全标准","usage":""}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9869&scene=%E5%AA%92%E4%BD%93%E7%A7%91%E6%8A%80&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9868","type":"writing","title":"食物需求增加","book":"密题范文-大作文","part":2,"description":"Task 2 · 至少 250 词","minWords":250,"prompt":"Demand for food is increasing worldwide.\nWhat are the causes?\nWhat measures could the international community take in order to ensure enough food supply?","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">Demand for food is increasing worldwide.<br>What are the causes?<br>What measures could the international community take in order to ensure enough food supply?<br>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.<br>Write at least 250 words.</div><p>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.</p><p><br/></p><p>Write at least 250 words.</p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website_with_ai_corrections","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"The growing global demand for food, driven primarily by population growth and changing diets, presents a formidable challenge to modern society. This essay will examine the primary causes behind this crisis and outline feasible strategies for the international community to address it effectively.\nOne major driver of rising food demand is rapid demographic expansion. With the global population having already surpassed eight billion, traditional agricultural systems face unprecedented pressure to satisfy basic human nutritional needs. Furthermore, as incomes rise in many regions, consumers tend to buy more animal products and a wider variety of foods. Producing meat and dairy products requires feed as well as resources for raising animals. Changes in diet can therefore increase pressure on agricultural production beyond the direct effect of population growth.\nTo tackle these dual challenges, a comprehensive and proactive approach is essential. First, international collaboration must be prioritized to accelerate agricultural innovation and climate resilience. Nations should share cutting-edge farming technologies, including drought-resistant crop varieties, vertical farming, and precision irrigation techniques. For instance, dryland farming technologies developed in arid regions can be transferred to vulnerable developing countries to secure local yields. Second, global efforts should focus on reducing food loss and waste across the supply chain. By improving refrigeration storage infrastructure in developing regions and reforming food consumption habits in developed economies, a substantial portion of the world's food supply can be preserved without increasing environmental strain.\nIn conclusion, the global food crisis is the combined result of population pressure and changing consumption patterns. By fostering international cooperation in agricultural technology and taking decisive action to curb food waste, the global community can build a more resilient and sustainable food system for the future.","word_count":280,"revision_notes":["driven primarily by population growth and climate change → driven primarily by population growth and changing diets","Furthermore, climate change severely exacerbates this pressure by disrupting global food production. Extreme weather events—such as prolonged droughts, severe flooding, and unpredictable seasonal shifts—frequently destroy harvests, destabilize global food supply chains, and trigger localized famine and price spikes. → Furthermore, as incomes rise in many regions, consumers tend to buy more animal products and a wider variety of foods. Producing meat and dairy products requires feed as well as resources for raising animals. Changes in diet can therefore increase pressure on agricultural production beyond the direct effect of population growth.","the combined result of population pressure and climate disruption → the combined result of population pressure and changing consumption patterns"]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["按两个问题分别分析需求上升原因和国际社会如何保障供应；可写人口增长与饮食变化。","措施强调国际合作：分享农业技术、资助储存运输、减少供应链浪费，并说明如何提高供给。","气候变化主要影响供应，不直接等同于需求增长；将问题的两个方向分清，避免虚构统计。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"food demand","meaning_zh":"粮食需求","usage":""},{"expression":"population growth","meaning_zh":"人口增长","usage":""},{"expression":"agricultural productivity","meaning_zh":"农业生产率","usage":""},{"expression":"food waste","meaning_zh":"食物浪费","usage":""},{"expression":"supply chain","meaning_zh":"供应链","usage":""},{"expression":"resource efficiency","meaning_zh":"资源利用效率","usage":""}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9868&scene=%E7%8E%AF%E5%A2%83&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9862","type":"writing","title":"所有阶段学费全免","book":"密题范文-大作文","part":2,"description":"Task 2 · 至少 250 词","minWords":250,"prompt":"Some people think that governments should provide free education at all levels, including primary school, secondary school and university. Others believe that students should pay for their own tuition fees. Discuss both views and give your own opinion.","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">Some people think that governments should provide free education at all levels, including primary school, secondary school and university. Others believe that students should pay for their own tuition fees. Discuss both views and give your own opinion.<br>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.<br>Write at least 250 words.</div><p>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.</p><p><br/></p><p>Write at least 250 words.</p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"Many governments across the world are struggling to find an answer to the question of whether they should cover tuition fees for education at all levels. While I acknowledge the benefits of governments providing free education for their citizens, I believe a fairer approach would be for governments and the public to share the cost of education, particularly at university level.\nOn the one hand, fully funded education by the government does offer many benefits, not only to individuals but also to society as a whole. The most notable benefit is that it can promote educational equality. It is widely acknowledged that tuition fees can place a heavy financial burden on low-income families. When poor families struggle to find a way out in a competitive world, some children may be forced to leave school early and enter the workforce. If governments provide free education, children from disadvantaged backgrounds can have access to schools regardless of their families’ financial circumstances. They can acquire essential knowledge and skills, eventually becoming productive members of society and having a better chance of realising their full potential.\nOn the other hand, some people hold the view that students should be responsible for at least part of their own tuition fees, particularly when pursuing higher education. Firstly, providing free education at all levels would place a considerable financial burden on governments. They would have to cover teachers’ salaries, facilities and equipment, which could leave fewer public funds available for other essential areas such as healthcare and infrastructure. In addition, requiring university students to contribute towards their tuition fees can encourage greater financial responsibility and reduce their dependence on public funding. Since higher education can bring substantial personal benefits, such as better employment opportunities and higher future earnings, it is reasonable for students to bear part of its cost rather than relying entirely on taxpayers.\nIn conclusion, free education can provide equal educational opportunities for everyone, especially children from low-income families. However, government budgets are limited, and higher education can generate significant private benefits. Therefore, I believe that governments should fully support basic education while requiring university students to contribute a reasonable proportion of their tuition fees.","word_count":360,"revision_notes":[]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["区分免费教育的公平价值与财政承受能力，再回应所有教育阶段的范围。","免费或资助可降低家庭负担；无限制全免可能挤压教育质量，需比较定向补助。","选择明确立场并覆盖高等教育；不把免学费等同于所有生活费用全免。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"tuition fees","meaning_zh":"学费","usage":""},{"expression":"equal access","meaning_zh":"平等获得机会","usage":""},{"expression":"public funding","meaning_zh":"公共资助","usage":""},{"expression":"targeted financial aid","meaning_zh":"定向经济援助","usage":""},{"expression":"educational quality","meaning_zh":"教育质量","usage":""},{"expression":"fiscal pressure","meaning_zh":"财政压力","usage":""}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9862&scene=%E6%95%99%E8%82%B2&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9861","type":"writing","title":"换新VS修旧","book":"密题范文-大作文","part":2,"description":"Task 2 · 至少 250 词","minWords":250,"prompt":"In many parts of the world, people now often throw things away when they are broken and buy new ones, whereas in the past broken things were repaired and used again.\nWhy do you think this is the case?\nWhat problems may it lead to?","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">In many parts of the world, people now often throw things away when they are broken and buy new ones, whereas in the past broken things were repaired and used again.<br>Why do you think this is the case?<br>What problems may it lead to?<br>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.<br>Write at least 250 words.</div><p>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.</p><p><br/></p><p>Write at least 250 words.</p><p><br/></p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"In many parts of the world, it has become common for people to throw away damaged items and buy new ones, whereas in the past, broken things were usually repaired. In my opinion, this change is mainly caused by cheap mass-produced goods and rapid technological updates, and it leads to severe environmental pollution and financial stress for individuals.\nThere are two primary reasons why people prefer replacing broken items to repairing them. Firstly, mass production lowers the cost of new goods, while manual repair services have become expensive. Modern assembly lines significantly reduce the manufacturing costs of electronics and furniture, making the price of buying a brand-new product very affordable. In contrast, labor fees and replacement parts are often too high, making replacement far more cost-effective. Secondly, consumerism and rapid technological updates encourage people to buy the latest models. Companies frequently release new items with updated features and attractive advertising. As a result, when an old product breaks, consumers prefer upgrading to a newer model rather than spending time and money repairing the old one.\nHowever, this growing trend brings serious negative consequences. The most significant problem is that throwing away broken goods creates huge amounts of waste and harms the environment. Large numbers of discarded electronics and plastic items cannot decompose naturally, which leads to overflowing landfills and toxic emissions. For instance, electronic waste releases hazardous chemicals that pollute soil and water. Furthermore, frequent purchases increase personal financial stress and foster a wasteful lifestyle. Buying new products continuously drains household income, putting extra economic pressure on average families. Over time, this habit also weakens the traditional virtue of thrift and encourages irresponsible consumption.\nIn conclusion, the tendency to discard broken items is largely driven by low product prices and fast technological advances. This habit creates critical environmental problems through excessive waste and places an unnecessary financial burden on individuals.","word_count":310,"revision_notes":[]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["两个任务是解释为什么人们更倾向换新，再说明这一趋势导致的问题。","原因可写新商品便宜、维修费用高和产品更新快；问题写垃圾增加、资源浪费与家庭额外开支。","主体段分别对应原因与问题，用同一物品例子说明机制；解决措施不应挤占题目要求。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"repair costs","meaning_zh":"维修成本","usage":""},{"expression":"product lifespan","meaning_zh":"产品寿命","usage":""},{"expression":"electronic waste","meaning_zh":"电子垃圾","usage":""},{"expression":"planned obsolescence","meaning_zh":"计划性淘汰","usage":""},{"expression":"consumer behaviour","meaning_zh":"消费者行为","usage":""},{"expression":"cost-effective solution","meaning_zh":"合算的解决方案","usage":""}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9861&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E7%94%9F%E6%B4%BB&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9825","type":"writing","title":"超市营业时间","book":"密题范文-大作文","part":2,"description":"Task 2 · 至少 250 词","minWords":250,"prompt":"In some countries, more and more shops are open long hours every day of the week.\nIs it a positive or negative development for shoppers and local community?","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">In some countries, more and more shops are open long hours every day of the week.<br>Is it a positive or negative development for shoppers and local community?<br>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.<br>Write at least 250 words.</div><p>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.</p><p><br/></p><p>Write at least 250 words.</p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"In many countries today, an increasing number of retail shops remain open for long hours every day of the week. While this trend provides undeniable convenience for consumers and boosts shop revenues, it also brings significant disadvantages regarding rising operational costs and low returns on investment. In my opinion, this is a mixed development for shoppers and local communities.\nOn the one hand, extended shopping hours offer notable advantages for both consumers and businesses. Firstly, long opening hours provide great convenience for shoppers with busy or irregular schedules. Many modern people work long hours, and extended operating times allow busy workers to buy daily necessities late in the evening or during weekends without rushing. This flexibility significantly improves their overall quality of life. Secondly, staying open longer helps shops attract more customers, leading to higher sales and revenue. By extending their business hours, shops can cater to off-peak shoppers who would otherwise not visit, which directly increases daily sales and helps boost the local retail economy.\nOn the other hand, the negative impacts of this trend on local shop owners and workforce management cannot be ignored. To begin with, operating longer hours raises businesses' overall expenses and increases employee workloads. Keeping a store open late requires extra utility bills for electricity and heating, as well as hiring additional staff or paying overtime to current workers. This places a heavy financial burden on small local businesses. Furthermore, low customer traffic during late-night hours can lead to a poor return on investment. On late weeknights, the number of shoppers visiting physical stores is usually very small. As a result, the minimal revenue generated during these hours cannot cover the high operational costs, leading to a waste of commercial resources.\nIn conclusion, having shops open for long hours every day is a development with both benefits and drawbacks. Although it offers shoppers flexibility and provides businesses with opportunities to increase revenue, the pressure of high labor costs and poor late-night profits presents real challenges for local communities.","word_count":334,"revision_notes":[]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["按题目要求评价延长超市营业时间对消费者、员工和商家的影响。","消费者获得便利；员工轮班、能源费用和小店竞争构成成本。","立场可支持适度延时并保障休息，解释为什么条件能缓解问题。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"extended opening hours","meaning_zh":"延长营业时间","usage":""},{"expression":"consumer convenience","meaning_zh":"消费者便利","usage":""},{"expression":"shift work","meaning_zh":"轮班工作","usage":""},{"expression":"operating costs","meaning_zh":"运营成本","usage":""},{"expression":"work-life balance","meaning_zh":"工作与生活平衡","usage":""},{"expression":"employee welfare","meaning_zh":"员工福利","usage":""}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9825&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E7%94%9F%E6%B4%BB&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9824","type":"writing","title":"明星的榜样作用","book":"密题范文-大作文","part":2,"description":"Task 2 · 至少 250 词","minWords":250,"prompt":"Famous people are regarded as role models to the young.\nDo you think this is a positive or negative development?","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">Famous people are regarded as role models to the young.<br>Do you think this is a positive or negative development?<br>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.<br>Write at least 250 words.</div><p>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.</p><p><br/></p><p>Write at least 250 words.</p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"In modern society, famous people are often regarded as role models for the younger generation. In my opinion, this is a mixed development. While celebrities can inspire young people through their perseverance and charitable work, the negative impact of their unhealthy lifestyles and materialistic values cannot be ignored.\nOn the one hand, celebrities can exert a positive influence on young people’s personal growth and social responsibility. Firstly, athletes and successful individuals inspire youth with their positive attitudes and perseverance. When athletes demonstrate hard work and determination in competitions, young people admire these traits and emulate them. This helps them build a positive mindset to overcome personal challenges in their studies and daily life. Secondly, celebrities participating in charitable events encourage young followers to act kindly. Many famous figures use their influence to support charity work, and these philanthropic actions are widely reported by the media. This inspires young fans to develop empathy and actively contribute to society.\nOn the other hand, the negative influence of celebrities on young people is equally significant. For one thing, the materialistic lifestyles showcased by some famous figures promote unhealthy consumerism. Some celebrities frequently display luxury goods and high-spending habits on social media, which easily causes young people to engage in unrealistic comparisons. Consequently, they may develop distorted values and spend excessively beyond their financial capacity. Furthermore, misbehavior by public figures can lead to bad habits among young fans. Because young people are not fully mature and lack critical thinking, they might view behaviors like irregular routines or alcohol abuse as cool, leading them to copy these habits and harm their physical health.\nIn conclusion, I believe that celebrities acting as role models is a development with both benefits and drawbacks. Although famous people can promote perseverance and social responsibility, the risks of spreading materialism and bad habits are severe. Parents and schools should guide young people to think critically and choose truly positive role models.","word_count":321,"revision_notes":[]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["承认明星的示范影响，比较其公益或自律行为与不良行为带来的作用。","说明年轻人模仿的机制，再举一种积极行为和一种风险，并联系媒介素养。","避免以个别明星推断全部明星；观点保持与原题讨论范围一致。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"role model","meaning_zh":"榜样","usage":""},{"expression":"public influence","meaning_zh":"公众影响力","usage":""},{"expression":"social responsibility","meaning_zh":"社会责任","usage":""},{"expression":"media literacy","meaning_zh":"媒介素养","usage":""},{"expression":"impressionable teenagers","meaning_zh":"易受影响的青少年","usage":""},{"expression":"charitable activities","meaning_zh":"慈善活动","usage":""}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9824&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E7%94%9F%E6%B4%BB&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9819","type":"writing","title":"限制员工互相交流","book":"密题范文-大作文","part":2,"description":"Task 2 · 至少 250 词","minWords":250,"prompt":"In many countries, some companies restrict communication between employees.\nWhy is this happening?\nIs this a positive or negative development?","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">In many countries, some companies restrict communication between employees.<br>Why is this happening?<br>Is this a positive or negative development?<br>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.<br>Write at least 250 words.</div><p>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.</p><p style=\"font-family: Arial !important; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; flex-wrap: wrap; text-wrap-mode: initial !important;\"><br/></p><p style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px; flex-wrap: wrap; font-family: Arial !important; text-wrap-mode: initial !important;\">Write at least 250 words.</p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website_with_ai_corrections","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"In recent years, an increasing number of enterprises have implemented strict policies to limit communication among their staff. This phenomenon is primarily driven by the desire to increase productivity and safeguard sensitive data. Although these restrictions may offer some short-term advantages, I firmly believe that this is a largely negative development due to its detrimental effects on teamwork and employee morale.\nThere are two main reasons why companies decide to control internal communication. First, managers believe that restricting non-work-related interactions helps minimize distractions and boost overall productivity. When employees engage in casual social chats during office hours, their focus is easily fragmented, which disrupts their workflow and delays project deadlines. Second, data security is a primary concern for modern businesses. Many organizations handle confidential commercial secrets, financial records, or private customer information. Allowing unmonitored communication across various channels increases the risk of accidental data leaks, prompting companies to impose strict controls to protect their intellectual property.\nAdmittedly, regulating communication can have a positive impact by fostering a quiet atmosphere suitable for deep, focused work. With fewer workplace interruptions and noise, employees can process complex tasks with higher accuracy. However, I consider this policy to be a predominantly negative trend. Overly restrictive rules severely hinder effective team collaboration, as they prevent staff members from sharing ideas and brainstorming solutions. Furthermore, a silent and overly controlled environment creates a cold, tense workplace culture. This lack of social connection lowers job satisfaction, increases stress levels, and ultimately leads to high employee turnover rates.\nIn conclusion, companies restrict staff communication mainly to prevent distraction and secure confidential information. While this approach may create a quiet work environment for short-term focus, its long-term harms to collaboration and employee well-being far outweigh the benefits.","word_count":288,"revision_notes":["I firm believe → I firmly believe"]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["本题既问公司限制员工交流的原因，也问这是积极还是消极发展。","先分析减少干扰与保护机密的动机，再比较专注收益和协作、士气损失。","明确总体评价，区分与工作相关的交流和闲聊；提出折中办法时仍要回答正负判断。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"workplace communication","meaning_zh":"职场交流","usage":""},{"expression":"team collaboration","meaning_zh":"团队协作","usage":""},{"expression":"employee morale","meaning_zh":"员工士气","usage":""},{"expression":"workplace distraction","meaning_zh":"工作干扰","usage":""},{"expression":"knowledge sharing","meaning_zh":"知识共享","usage":""},{"expression":"reasonable restrictions","meaning_zh":"合理限制","usage":""}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9819&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E7%94%9F%E6%B4%BB&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9814","type":"writing","title":"教育与犯罪","book":"密题范文-大作文","part":2,"description":"Task 2 · 至少 250 词","minWords":250,"prompt":"In many countries, prison is the most common solution to the problem of crime. However, another effective way is to provide people with better education so that they will not become criminals.\nTo what extent do you agree or disagree?","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">In many countries, prison is the most common solution to the problem of crime. However, another effective way is to provide people with better education so that they will not become criminals.<br>To what extent do you agree or disagree?<br>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.<br>Write at least 250 words.</div><p>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.</p><p><br/></p><p>Write at least 250 words.</p><p><br/></p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"It is often argued that expanding educational opportunities is a more effective way to reduce crime rates than relying heavily on imprisonment. While I agree that education plays a vital role in addressing the root causes of crime, I believe that prisons remain indispensable for punishing serious offenses and maintaining public safety.\nOn the one hand, providing quality education is an effective long-term strategy to prevent people from engaging in illegal activities. Firstly, education equips individuals with practical skills and qualifications, enabling them to secure stable employment and a reliable income. As a result, people who can earn an honest living are far less likely to commit property crimes, such as theft or burglary, out of economic hardship. Secondly, moral and civic education in schools fosters a strong sense of social responsibility. When young people learn to respect the law and understand the consequences of their actions, they are less inclined to display anti-social behavior.\nOn the other hand, education alone cannot completely eliminate crime, which makes prisons necessary. The primary reason is that correctional facilities serve as a powerful deterrent to potential offenders. The fear of losing personal freedom effectively deters individuals from committing severe or premeditated crimes, such as robbery or assault. Furthermore, prisons play a crucial role in isolating dangerous criminals from society. Without incarceration, violent repeat offenders would remain on the streets, posing a constant threat to public safety regardless of any educational programs available.\nIn conclusion, I partly agree with the statement. While education is an essential preventive measure that tackles the economic and moral roots of crime, prisons are still necessary as an immediate deterrent and protective mechanism against severe offenses.","word_count":277,"revision_notes":[]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["回应教育能否预防犯罪的观点，比较预防作用与监狱的惩罚、隔离作用。","教育改善就业与法律意识；监狱对严重暴力犯罪仍有保护公众的作用。","可部分同意：教育减少风险但不能完全代替刑罚，避免将教育写成必然消除犯罪。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"vocational training","meaning_zh":"职业培训","usage":""},{"expression":"employment opportunities","meaning_zh":"就业机会","usage":""},{"expression":"rehabilitation","meaning_zh":"改造与重返社会","usage":""},{"expression":"legal awareness","meaning_zh":"法律意识","usage":""},{"expression":"reoffending","meaning_zh":"再次犯罪","usage":""},{"expression":"social integration","meaning_zh":"社会融入","usage":""}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9814&scene=%E7%8A%AF%E7%BD%AA&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9813","type":"writing","title":"文盲率高的原因和措施","book":"密题范文-大作文","part":2,"description":"Task 2 · 至少 250 词","minWords":250,"prompt":"Despite better access to education, many adults today still cannot read or write.\nIn what ways are they disadvantaged?\nWhat can governments do to help them?","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">Despite better access to education, many adults today still cannot read or write.<br>In what ways are they disadvantaged?<br>What can governments do to help them?<br>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.<br>Write at least 250 words.</div><p>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Write at least 250 words.</p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"Despite improvements in educational access, illiteracy remains a major challenge for many adults around the world. These individuals face significant disadvantages in their daily lives, but governments can take targeted actions to help them overcome these obstacles.\nAdults who cannot read or write face severe limitations in both their personal and professional lives. Economically, they are largely excluded from the modern job market, as even entry-level positions often require basic literacy skills. Consequently, they are often restricted to low-paying manual labor, leaving them vulnerable to financial hardship. Socially, basic tasks such as reading public notices, filling out official forms, or following medical instructions become daunting challenges. This inability to navigate daily transactions not only undermines their self-confidence but can also put their health and safety at risk.\nTo address this issue, governments should implement comprehensive strategies to support illiterate adults. First, public funding should be allocated to set up free, community-based adult literacy programs. These classes ought to offer flexible schedules, such as evening or weekend sessions, allowing working adults to attend without compromising their livelihoods. Second, governments should raise public awareness to reduce the social stigma surrounding adult illiteracy. By offering anonymous learning channels or integrating literacy training into workplace development schemes, adults would feel more comfortable seeking help without fear of embarrassment.\nIn conclusion, illiterate adults are seriously disadvantaged in terms of employment opportunities and daily independence. However, through fully funded adult education programs and supportive social policies, governments can effectively empower these individuals to improve their literacy skills and quality of life.","word_count":255,"revision_notes":[]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["按英文原题回答成人不识字的劣势与政府帮助措施，题目没有要求分析文盲产生原因。","劣势可写求职受限、无法独立填表或阅读指示；措施为免费灵活课程、工作场所学习和减少污名。","用政府资金、社区机构和夜间课程说明执行方式，将每项帮助对应一种困难。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"adult literacy","meaning_zh":"成人读写能力","usage":""},{"expression":"school dropout","meaning_zh":"辍学","usage":""},{"expression":"educational access","meaning_zh":"教育机会","usage":""},{"expression":"flexible learning","meaning_zh":"灵活学习","usage":""},{"expression":"community-based programmes","meaning_zh":"社区课程","usage":""},{"expression":"basic literacy skills","meaning_zh":"基础读写技能","usage":""}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9813&scene=%E6%95%99%E8%82%B2&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-writing-9812","type":"writing","title":"传统课程被替代","book":"密题范文-大作文","part":2,"description":"Task 2 · 至少 250 词","minWords":250,"prompt":"The typical teaching situation of a teacher and students in the class will not exist by the year 2050.\nTo what extent do you agree or disagree?","passage":"<div class=\"original-prompt\">The typical teaching situation of a teacher and students in the class will not exist by the year 2050.<br>To what extent do you agree or disagree?<br>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.<br>Write at least 250 words.</div><p>Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your knowledge and experience.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Write at least 250 words.</p>","questions":[],"supportSections":[{"id":"model_answer","title":"参考范文","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"text":"It is predicted that by the year 2050, the typical teaching situation involving a teacher and students in a physical classroom will no longer exist. In my opinion, I partially agree with this view. While online platforms and AI will significantly reshape how knowledge is delivered, physical classrooms and human teachers will not completely disappear.\nOn the one hand, emerging technologies bring massive benefits that make self-directed learning far more accessible and flexible. Firstly, online resources and AI can offer tailored learning materials for self-study. The internet provides a vast amount of educational content, and intelligent software can analyze a student's weak points to recommend precise study plans. As a result, students can acquire knowledge efficiently on their own without relying entirely on traditional lectures. Secondly, online learning allows students to study anytime and anywhere with high efficiency. Without the need to commute to physical classrooms every day, learners have full control over their study schedules. This flexibility saves valuable time and improves overall efficiency.\nOn the other hand, traditional teaching setups remain irreplaceable for essential non-academic reasons. For one thing, human teachers are irreplaceable in providing moral education and emotional care. Education is far more than transmitting textbook facts; it involves building correct values and good character. Real teachers can observe students' emotions, offer timely encouragement, and teach them right from wrong, which cold machines cannot do. Furthermore, physical classrooms support deeper real-time interaction and social connection. Being in the same physical space allows teachers and students to engage in spontaneous face-to-face discussions. This real-time feedback encourages critical thinking while helping young learners build vital social skills with their peers.\nIn conclusion, I partially agree that traditional teaching setups will undergo profound changes by 2050. Online tools and AI will certainly replace the traditional teacher-led lecture model by offering flexible learning opportunities. However, because human teachers are essential for moral guidance and real-time interaction, physical classrooms will continue to exist in a modified form.","word_count":325,"revision_notes":[]}},{"id":"writing_ideas","title":"写作思路","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"points":["判断2050年前传统课堂是否完全消失，并明确赞同程度。","承认线上学习和AI带来灵活与个性化；再写教师情感支持、面对面互动和实践课程的作用。","区分教学形式改变与课堂完全消失，避免把题目写成简单的线上学习优缺点。"]}},{"id":"recommended_vocabulary","title":"推荐词汇","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"expression":"physical classroom","meaning_zh":"实体课堂","usage":""},{"expression":"personalised learning","meaning_zh":"个性化学习","usage":""},{"expression":"self-directed learning","meaning_zh":"自主学习","usage":""},{"expression":"face-to-face interaction","meaning_zh":"面对面交流","usage":""},{"expression":"emotional support","meaning_zh":"情感支持","usage":""},{"expression":"blended learning","meaning_zh":"混合式学习","usage":""}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/answerWritingEassy?topicId=9812&scene=%E6%95%99%E8%82%B2&smarterPracticeRecordId=&batchNo=&showFloatButton=false&isEssay=true","note":"网站参考内容与 AI 建议分别标注，非官方评分答案"},"library":true}]);